C, the chaotic male elven wizard, died on dungeon level 8 [max 9],
killed by a giant spider.  He was level 4.

...A little bit about me, the nethack player:  I have been playing a
few months.  I am spoiled.  I am fairly cautious, and haven't got much
below dungeon level 10 with my best characters (usually they are
around 10th level and exploring Mine's End when they bite it)....

So we enter with our fearless hero on DL 3. He knows force bolt and
detect food spells.  He has a cool +3 goblin helm.  Lo and behold, a
general store.  C begins to price ID a pretty decent range of potions
and scrolls.  Things are looking good.  C explores the rest of the
level and finds the Gnomish minds entrance.  Good Good.  He is still
level 1, however he has a nice big fat housecat.  He picks up a couple
more items and head back to ID them at the store.

In the meantime, a gas spore seems to have materialized inside, and
(unthinkingly!) C blasts it with a force bolt (me, the nethack player
can get impatient late at nite).  Shopkeeper is standing nearby (2
squares away) and gets angry, C raises his level to 2.  Uh oh.  C
would not be the first to die from an angry shopkeeper.  What does he
do?  Shuts the door, first of all.  That seems like a good idea.  The
shopkeeper doesn't seem to come out.

 I decide ( I know I know) to save my game and make a copy ( I am
still learning, y'know, this game is HARD).  C can't remember if he
can bribe him to calm down, so he opens the door to try, at least
better than taking a force bolt to the back of the head.  Shopkeeper
zaps C with about 5 or 6 magic missiles.  Cloak resists wonderfully.
C remembers that in his starting equipment was a Wand of Teleport.  He
zaps it at the 'keeper.  "Brilliant" he says to himself, loots the
shop, and leaves to the nearby downstairs with his 'cat.

A very short time later, while early into DL 4, C steps on a trap
door, and plummets to DL 9!!!!  Of course the cat was not next to
him.  "This is not good" he says.  Not good at all.  He quickly
locates the upstairs, takes it back to 8.  Locates a scroll shop!? and
purchases two ID scrolls and an enchant armor...B/U/C unknown.  I
utilized these, but in the end only ended up with a -1 uncursed cloak
of magic resistance (I had a remove curse when the EA cursed it)

As the story nears its fateful end, C gets a weird feeling about
psychic energies on the level ( 8 still)...hmm, as a nethack player I
have not seen that message before...and a short time later something
seems to suck at his brain....he is really scared now...He opens the
door to the next room and there is a purple letter h staring at him,
with the word 'master' in front of it.  Oh yea, a big hunting tiger is
in the room too.  "Oh crap!", C zaps the wand at himself...he is
teleported almost NEXT to the mmf.  "#($FD!!", <zap> a second time,
and he is teleported more or less to where he expects the upstairs
will be...he is at 2 life...he rounds a corner...a Giant Spider sees
him, attacks him, and C breathes his final breaths.

Did RNG have it in for him!?  or was he penalized for looting the shop
and making the 'keeper furious?  I added his level (4 when he died,
although he was 3 when he entered that fateful level 8) to the DL and
I do not see HOW a mmf gets generated on that level on accident.  As
it is I have not seen a trap door take a character down 5 levels!

I admit I was in a rush at the end, and could have possibly found the
upstairs and escaped to 7...but in the back of my mind C was already
dead...Too high a mountain to climb (at least for my skills).  Tips?
Could I have Elbereth'ed a bunch of times, healed, and steered clear
of trouble? I bet there were a horde of killer bees or ants waiting
for me in the stairwell.

Hope you were entertained...



